{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a sorted set or sorted dictionary by the workload it will see."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sorted sets share one API: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"text":"’s set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operations, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowerBound(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"upperBound(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(in:)"},{"text":", and the elements as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank. Changing which one a program uses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a change of type name:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let avl: AVLTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let redBlack: RedBlackTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let bTree: BTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let skipList: SkipList = [40, 10, 30, 20]","","Array(avl)              \/\/ [10, 20, 30, 40], and the same for the others","avl.lowerBound(25)      \/\/ 2, the index of 30","bTree.lowerBound(25)    \/\/ 2"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one takes O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") per lookup, insertion and removal (expected for the treap and skip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list, amortized for the splay tree). They differ in the constant, in what else they offer, and in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which workloads they suit."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Lookups-and-scans-over-a-large-set-BTree","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Lookups and scans over a large set: BTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A B-tree node (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") holds tens of elements side by side, so a lookup reads a few nodes and few","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cache lines, and iteration walks contiguous arrays. For a large set that is read far more often","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than it is changed, and for range scans, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the default. Copying a B-tree shares its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nodes, and a mutated copy copies only the nodes on the path it changes. ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its sorted dictionary.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Balanced-binary-trees-AVLTree-and-RedBlackTree","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Balanced binary trees: AVLTree and RedBlackTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLTree"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the heights of every vertex’s subtrees within one of each other, so it is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shallowest of the binary trees and the quickest of them to search. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RedBlackTree"},{"type":"text","text":" allows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taller tree and in return rotates at most two or three times per insertion or removal; prefer it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when changes outnumber lookups. Both convert to a Grafluent "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"type":"text","text":" that shows the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary in an AVL tree."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Splitting-and-joining-Treap","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Splitting and joining: Treap"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a random priority on each vertex, which makes its shape a random binary search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree’s whatever order the elements arrive in, and gives it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"split(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"join(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"OverlappingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the sets interleave. Pass a seeded generator to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Treap(_:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to make every shape reproducible. ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splits too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-working-set-of-hot-elements-SplayTree","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"A working set of hot elements: SplayTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps no balance information. "},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and each mutation rotate the element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they reach to the root, so a run of lookups that keeps returning to a few elements finds them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"near the top:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its other reads, "},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" among them, leave the tree as it is, so they keep value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantics; use "},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" where the splay is wanted."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-sorted-queue-with-a-simple-structure-SkipList","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"A sorted queue with a simple structure: SkipList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A skip list (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") stacks sorted linked levels, each holding about half the elements of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the one below. Its insertions touch only the levels an element reaches, and its levels are a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent graph through ","type":"text"},{"code":"layersView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Keeping-every-version-PersistentTreeSet","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Keeping every version: PersistentTreeSet"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When old versions must stay readable, as in undo histories, snapshots handed to other tasks or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backtracking searches, a persistent set (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") shares all but the vertices an edit touched:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let empty = PersistentTreeSet<Int>()","let one = empty.inserting(5)","let two = one.inserting(3)","let three = two.removing(5)","Array(one)                    \/\/ [5]","Array(two)                    \/\/ [3, 5]","Array(three)                  \/\/ [3]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each version costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") new vertices rather than a copy of the whole tree."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PersistentTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Summary","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Summary"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Workload","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Large sets, mostly lookups, range scans","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mostly lookups, a binary shape to inspect","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLTree"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mostly insertions and removals","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RedBlackTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splitting and joining sets"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Repeated access to a few elements","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SplayTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every version kept"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PersistentTreeSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistentTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A simple sorted queue"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkipList"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/choosingasearchtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"generated":true}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"title":"Choosing a search tree","role":"article"},"references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/RangeAndSpatialTrees":{"abstract":[{"text":"Answer queries over ranges of a sequence, over intervals, and over points in space.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/rangeandspatialtrees","title":"Range and spatial trees","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph","title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","type":"topic","role":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/btrees":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","title":"BTrees","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"BTrees","type":"codeVoice"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","abstract":[{"text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","role":"article","title":"Tries and suffix structures","type":"topic"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/DecisionDiagrams":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/decisiondiagrams","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represent Boolean functions and families of sets as shared, canonical graphs."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Decision diagrams"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/skiplists":{"title":"SkipLists","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkipLists"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/persistenttrees":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","title":"PersistentTrees","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTrees"}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","title":"GrafluentCollections","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}